rota lap 4624, row 0 -- Aether, the row that hears; advanced by hand past row 4, which the previous lap read. The threshold page asks the lap to listen for the silence where a claim used to be, and all three repairs below are one silence: a guard that refuses and lets the reader hear nothing about what refused.
think Cold roster pass read two reds, shim_reason and standing_equipment. The second is downstream -- its scan reads the run card's recorded verdicts, so it reds while any rostered guard does.
think shim_reason named its cause exactly: tools/g/gitlink_dependent_witness.rish binds the scan at line 61 and says scan.out at line 88, below the first assert on that binding at 64. An assert ends the run in Rishi, so on a refusing scan the reader receives the witness's own else message and never the scan's report. Moved the say above the first assert; late_say_rostered 1 -> 0, both witnesses GREEN.
think dated_path is the other standing red -- refs_lost 107 against a ceiling of 85. Its under_ceiling assert sat immediately under the census, above every control leg, so for as long as the field stood over its ceiling not one of that witness's controls ran. Moved the gate to the tail: same refusal, read after the instrument is proven.
think That reorder paid on its first run. It caught a genuine collision between my own corpus change and case three of the control, which plants an ordinary copied directory to prove the worktree exclusion is not a walker that never descends. The copy was untracked, so my filter removed it for a different reason and the leg would have proven the new filter twice and the elder exclusion not at all. Case three stages the copy now.
think Two real defects inside dated_path. First: the walker is grep -r ., so the citing corpus was the filesystem while the existence oracle was git ls-files. The scan's own comment already says a meter whose reading depends on untracked scratch is measuring the bench, and it reached worktrees alone. .lap/ is gitignored and one per checkout, and .lap/mine/convergence_tree_prove.sh fed a gone reading into a gate held at a ceiling -- eight ships answering one meter differently for a reason none of them could see. The corpus is keyed on git ls-files now; a page rejoins the moment it is staged, which is before the hot pass every send runs.
think Second: one living stale citation. tools/a/ascii_resident_agree_witness.rish cited external-research/20260910-081500_a-process-per-file.md; path_absence_scan reads it absent here and upstream, and the paper stands at 20260910-083451. A stamp typed from memory.
think The third room is the door the previous lap named: session_roster_agree builds a per-day report and prints it only under list, which its witness has never asked for. So a fleet pass reading stale=3 named no day. A count run about to read drift now prints the rows behind it, gated kinds only -- open_stale is a duty the day-close pays and a one-sided shelf at its ceiling is an honest reading, so neither is what refused. One predicate spells the naming and the verdict, so they cannot disagree.
obs dated_path stays red and I declined to move it. 100 of its 105 lost references are testimony accrete-never-break forbids anyone to repair, and lost_promised_living -- the repairable cell -- reads 0. The scan's own header already asks for the gate to move to that reading and says it waits on Keaton's word, because a gate a lap moves for itself is a ceiling raised by a side door. Named on the card instead.
obs No red could be booked in construction/REDS.md: the pin holds 40,945 of 40,960 bytes with every row OPEN, so there is no lawful room and no foldable row. All three findings are recorded on the card and here.
obs Every refusal is proven from both sides. The tracked-corpus filter was mutated away and the control leg read 2 where it reads 1, which is the reading an unfiltered walker gives -- so the leg tells the filter from its absence rather than from its presence alone.
